This directory has generic BLAS and LAPACK source files needed by the
ELECTRODE, ML-POD, ML-QUIP, ML-RUNNER, and RHEO packages (and
potentially by other packages in the future) that can be used instead of
platform or vendor optimized BLAS/LAPACK library.  The performance
difference is usually negligible, since the fraction of time spent
in the linear algebra calls is usually very small compared to the
rest of LAMMPS.

To simplify installation, these files have been translated from the
Fortran versions of the BLAS and LAPACK references source files at
https://netlib.org/lapack/ to C++ with f2c.  The package with the tools
to do the translation and the matching original Fortran sources are at
https://github.com/lammps/linalg.

Please note that even through the files are C++ source code the
resulting library will follow the Fortran binary interface conventions.

Note also that this is an *incomplete* subset of a full BLAS/LAPACK library.

The files correspond to LAPACK version 3.12.1.

You should only need to build and use the library in this directory if
you want to build LAMMPS with one of the listed packages AND you do not
have any other suitable BLAS and LAPACK libraries installed on your
system (like ATLAS, GOTO-BLAS, OpenBLAS, ACML, MKL and so on).
